        <detaileddescription>
<para>The relation <formula id="385">\[ \int_0^T \sigma_L^2(t)dt = \sigma_B^2 T \]</formula> holds, where <formula id="386">$ \sigma_L(t) $</formula> is the local volatility at time <formula id="147">$ t $</formula> and <formula id="387">$ \sigma_B(T) $</formula> is the Black volatility for maturity <formula id="45">$ T $</formula>. From the above, the formula <formula id="388">\[ \sigma_L(t) = \sqrt{\frac{\mathrm{d}}{\mathrm{d}t}\sigma_B^2(t)t} \]</formula> can be deduced which is here implemented. </para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
